    entity:merchandiser-resource-allocation a onto:Entity,
            class:project,
            owl:NamedIndividual,
            skos:Concept ;
        rdfs:label "Merchandiser Resource Allocation" ;
        fact:assumptions "Routes assigned to the same merchandiser must be on different days of the week and within the maximum allowed distance of each other; each merchandiser can take up to 6 routes" ;
        fact:business-context "Assign stores to specific visit schedules (e.g. MWF, TuTh) and plan daily routes to minimize the number of merchandisers needed and travel distance, with restrictions on visit frequency, duration, which stores can share a route, max travel distance and max working time",
            "Upcoming wage increase; lack of established processes for merchandiser allocation; existing process not optimal, causing inefficiencies in headcount, travel distance and time; need to efficiently deploy merchandisers to cover a large number of doors under various business restrictions" ;
        fact:business-need "Allocate merchandiser visits to stores while minimizing headcount and travel distance and maintaining proper service level for all stores; automate deployment planning and provide optimized routes to reduce cost and maximize coverage",
            "Minimize the number of merchandisers needed to cover all routes and reduce travel distances, while preventing overdeployment and underdeployment of field resources",
            "Minimize the number of merchandisers required and total travel distance while meeting every store's visit frequency and duration requirements" ;
        fact:delivery-evidence "Equal standards across the whole country by matching resources to store throughput, size and SKU variety; prevents overdeployment and underdeployment resulting in higher client satisfaction; optimized travel routes saving time and money; identification of areas for potential growth with minimal extra investment and of routes with spare capacity allowing more store coverage",
            "Estimated 30% headcount reduction overall (ranging from 1% to 41% depending on region); greedy method proved superior to other approaches on both time and quality",
            "Reduction in FTE requirements of 20% to 44% depending on regional characteristics; overall estimated headcount reduction of 30%; identification of new opportunities for coverage expansion" ;
        fact:project-summary "Case study on allocating merchandisers to store visit routes: minimize the number of merchandisers needed to cover all routes and minimize distances between routes assigned to the same merchandiser, subject to working-day and max-distance restrictions",
            "Merchandiser Resource Allocation project for Nestle Philippines: a tool that analyzes business restrictions, proximity, sales data and account information to generate optimized merchandiser deployment plans and routes, reducing cost and improving coverage and productivity" ;
        fact:proposed-solution "Simple greedy method: build an allowed-pairs-dict of route pairs on different days of week within max-distance, iterate over routes sorted ascending by frequency in the dict, and assign nearest compatible routes (sorted by distance ascending) to the same merchandiser up to 6 routes",
            "Three sequential optimization models: (1) assigning visit schedules to stores, (2) optimizing daily routes, (3) optimizing weekly schedules; innovative methodology allowing for high quality solutions while greatly reducing computational effort and time; delivered as a tool generating optimized deployment plans and most effective routes for merchandisers",
            "Two-stage optimization: Model #1 (store schedule assignment) uses binary variables indicating whether a store is assigned to a schedule plus auxiliary variables, requires every store to be assigned to a schedule, and balances daily demand spikes, political constraints, store proximity and schedule fitness; its output (stores to visit per day) feeds Model #2 (daily route optimization), a vehicle routing model minimizing total travel time/distance and number of merchandisers, with total time per merchandiser (travel + in-store) capped at 8 hours and political/route-compatibility constraints respected" ;
        fact:scope "Assignment of routes to merchandisers across the whole country, with constraints on number of working days and maximum distance allowed between routes assigned to the same merchandiser",
            "Optimization of merchandiser visit allocation to stores, daily route optimization and weekly schedule optimization based on proximity, sales and account information while respecting business restrictions",
            "Store-to-schedule assignment model and daily vehicle-routing model for merchandiser visits, implemented with the FICO Xpress Python library" ;
        fact:solution-direction "Operations research / heuristic optimization using a greedy assignment approach; capability pillars: ML Productization, Supply Chain Analytics, Statistics Exploration & Rules, Operations Research" ;
        fact:source-artifact-type "Case study",
            "pptx presentation converted to markdown (High level overview)" ;
        onto:kind "Project" ;
        relation:has-client entity:nestle-philippines ;
        relation:project-uses-technology entity:allowed-pairs-dict,
            entity:azure,
            entity:azure-maps,
            entity:databricks,
            entity:fico-xpress,
            entity:greedy-method,
            entity:or-tools,
            entity:power-bi,
            entity:python,
            entity:sql ;
        rdfs:comment "Project for Nestle Philippines using three sequential optimization models to allocate merchandiser visits to stores, optimize daily routes and weekly schedules, minimizing headcount and travel distance while maintaining service levels" ;
        skos:altLabel "Merchandiser Resource Allocation – High level overview",
            "Merchandiser allocation case study",
            "case study" ;
        skos:prefLabel "Merchandiser Resource Allocation" .

    entity:route-optimization-tool-proposal-for-cceap a onto:Entity,
            class:proposal,
            owl:NamedIndividual,
            skos:Concept ;
        rdfs:label "Route Optimization Tool proposal for CCEAP" ;
        fact:assumptions "No deep financial modeling required at this stage; demo stays high-level showcasing applicable routing capabilities" ;
        fact:business-context "No clear financial impact: routing inefficiencies not correlated to financial impact, making an ROI-led business case hard to build",
            "Route change drivers include promos, upsell priorities, weather, accidents and weekly tactical adjustments",
            "Sponsorship: business side - Director of Commercial Excellence; IT side - Abby Cenzon and Leiner Nebab. Lingaro sales contact: Jacq Marras. Client Q&A answered by Leiner Nebab on 2026-04-27." ;
        fact:business-need "Current tool is compliance-focused (tracks whether frontliners follow assigned routes) rather than optimization driven",
            "Difficult to ensure coverage of underserved territories while respecting territory boundaries",
            "Frontliners need clear, optimal routes considering traffic and distance; the Go-to-Market team needs nationwide planning with better visibility and control",
            "Highly manual process: frequent manual CSV uploads and manual lat-long adjustments, slow and error-prone updates",
            "Limited flexibility: current tool struggles to adapt to daily route changes driven by promos, upsell priorities, weather, accidents, weekly tactical adjustments",
            "Outdated platform (Windows XP-era, maps last updated around 2018-2019) resulting in inaccurate routing and poor usability",
            "Replace outdated, largely manual route planning (manual uploading of Excel/CSV files into an outdated, inflexible, non-intuitive tool with complex backend calculations requiring constant user input); challenges affect service levels (scheduled call list, route planning, route compliance), sales and volume delivery, and financials (no actual data yet). Initiative prompted by outdated platform, complexity of usage and manual interventions." ;
        fact:estimate-timeline "Possible RFP expected Q3 2026",
            "RFP possibly in Q3 2026" ;
        fact:exploration-backlog "Lingaro to review internally for similar routing optimization implementations or relevant use cases; assess whether Lingaro has demonstrable capabilities aligned to CCEAP's routing needs; prepare a high-level demo/presentation; CCEAP (Leiner) to involve GTM business stakeholders to review the demo" ;
        fact:lingaro-context "Lingaro (Jacq Marras) held an alignment meeting with CCEAP IT leads and circulated meeting minutes on 2026-05-04 summarizing key business pain points",
            "Lingaro (Jacq) to review internal routing optimization use cases and assess demonstrable capabilities aligned to CCEAP's routing needs" ;
        fact:proposal-stage "Early discovery; high-level demo/presentation to be prepared as input to decide on pilot/MVP and formal RFP",
            "Exploratory / vendor sourcing, pre-RFP",
            "Exploratory phase; client is sourcing for vendors" ;
        fact:proposal-status "Not yet funded; possible RFP expected in Q3 2026",
            "Still in exploratory phase; not yet funded; client currently sourcing vendors" ;
        fact:proposal-summary "Lingaro pursuing a Route Optimization Tool opportunity with Coca-Cola Philippines (CCEAP); client in exploratory phase sourcing vendors, possible RFP Q3 2026",
            "Replace CCEAP's outdated Windows XP-era routing tool with a modern route optimization tool; sponsored by the Director of Commercial Excellence (business side) with Abby Cenzon and Leiner Nebab as IT-side leads" ;
        fact:proposed-solution "Modern, flexible routing platform using updated maps (e.g. Google Maps 2024 or similar), supporting dynamic daily route adjustments and optimizing routes within assigned territories without penalizing valid deviations" ;
        fact:scope "Initial focus remains routing optimization; revenue impact considered secondary and potentially addressed later once routing basics are solved" ;
        fact:solution-direction "Provide insights on the fastest and most efficient way to complete weekly routes, better coverage of underserved areas, and real-time or near-real-time visibility on route compliance and execution" ;
        fact:target-context "CCEAP frontliners and Go-to-Market (GTM) team; GTM business stakeholders to review the demo/presentation" ;
        onto:kind "Proposal" ;
        relation:proposal-for-client entity:cceap ;
        relation:proposal-related-project entity:routing-pilot-mvp ;
        relation:proposal-source-note entity:meeting-minutes-email-re-route-optimization-tool ;
        relation:proposal-uses-technology entity:google-maps ;
        rdfs:comment "Lingaro proposal to Coca-Cola Philippines (CCEAP) for a route optimization tool to replace the outdated, largely manual routing process; client is in exploratory phase sourcing vendors, with a possible RFP in Q3 2026" ;
        skos:altLabel "Route Optimization Tool",
            "Routing platform",
            "routing optimization" ;
        skos:prefLabel "Route Optimization Tool proposal for CCEAP" .

    entity:cceap a onto:Entity,
            class:client,
            owl:NamedIndividual,
            skos:Concept ;
        rdfs:label "CCEAP" ;
        fact:business-context "Current platform maps are outdated, so reps manually check Google Maps on tablets; revenue optimization is not embedded in the routing tool and is handled separately by Finance",
            "Frontliner route consumption with daily / intra-day updates, GTM scenario planning, and KPI/compliance/coverage visibility across 11 commercial units",
            "GTM Team plans routes centrally, builds CSV files with manual lat-long adjustments per route and uploads/distributes weekly plans to sales reps; Sales Reps (pre-sellers and account developers) receive plans ahead of the working week and execute daily routes; Finance manages revenue and route revenue analysis separately with its own tooling, not integrated with the routing tool",
            "Sales reps receive weekly route plans ahead of the week; plans are uploaded to the routing tool via CSV files; manual intervention is required to adjust lat-long values, handle exceptions and daily changes, and adapt to weather, traffic, accidents or ad-hoc business needs",
            "Strict territory control: the 11 commercial units cannot cross territories; any deviation requires managerial judgement rather than system-guided optimization" ;
        fact:business-need "Exceptions and daily changes require manual intervention; ad-hoc changes (weather, traffic, accidents) handled with no system guidance; platform maps are outdated so reps check Google Maps manually; financial impact not embedded in routing decisions; territory-bound reps need manager approval for any deviation",
            "Frontliners need clear, optimal routes considering traffic and distance",
            "Go-To-Market team needs nationwide planning with better visibility and control",
            "Insights to surface: fastest and most efficient way to complete weekly routes; better coverage of underserved areas; real-time or near-real-time visibility on route compliance and execution" ;
        fact:client-description "Coca-Cola Philippines (CCEAP); frontliners and Go-to-Market team seeking a modern routing optimization platform",
            "Coca-Cola Philippines (CCEAP); route planning currently largely manual via Excel/file uploads into an outdated routing tool",
            "Coca-Cola Philippines (ccep.com) operating a field sales force (frontliners) whose routes are planned with an outdated routing platform",
            "Operates 11 commercial units with nationwide coverage under strict territory control; commercial units cannot cross territories and deviations require managerial judgement rather than system-guided optimization",
            "Organization whose Go-To-Market team plans routes centrally for nationwide coverage across 11 commercial units, with Frontliners (sales reps) executing weekly route plans" ;
        fact:client-summary "CCEAP: nationwide field sales operation with 11 commercial units, centrally planned weekly routes via CSV upload, strict territory control, and a routing platform with outdated maps and no Finance integration",
            "Exploring a Route Optimization Tool to replace legacy routing platform; business sponsor is the Director of Commercial Excellence, IT leads are Abby Cenzon and Leiner Nebab" ;
        fact:scope "Routing optimization within territory constraints for 11 commercial units nationwide; financial impact and revenue optimization out of initial scope (handled by Finance)" ;
        fact:solution-direction "Initial focus on routing optimization; revenue impact is secondary and potentially addressed later once routing basics are solved" ;
        fact:target-context "A modern, flexible routing platform using updated maps (e.g. Google Maps 2024 or similar), supporting dynamic daily route adjustments, optimizing routes within assigned territories without penalizing valid deviations, and serving both Frontliners and the Go-To-Market team" ;
